{"tool_name":"glycodigest","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"glycodigest","home":"http://www.glycodigest.org/","summary":"Tool that simulates the action of these exoglycosidases on released oligosaccharides. It assists glycobiologists in designing enzyme mixtures that can be used to guide the precise determination of glycan structures.","addition_date":"2017-12-06T18:14:09Z","last_update_date":"2019-09-04T08:38:47Z","tool_type":["Desktop application","Web application"],"collections":["Proteomics"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:glycodigest","credit":[{"email":"frederique.lisacek@isb-sib.ch","name":"Frederique Lisacek","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-0948-4537","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"matthew.campbell@mq.edu.au","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"ExPASy helpdesk","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://www.expasy.org/support"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/alternativeTime/unicarb_static/wiki/GlycoDigest-Guide-(UniCarbKB)"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["proteomics.bio.tools"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Molecular dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2476"}]},{"operation":[{"term":"Protein post-translation modification site prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0417"}]}],"name":"GlycoDigest","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"admin","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btu425","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 The Author 2014. Published by Oxford University Press.Sequencing oligosaccharides by exoglycosidases, either sequentially or in an array format, is a powerful tool to unambiguously determine the structure of complex N- and O-link glycans. Here, we introduce GlycoDigest, a tool that simulates exoglycosidase digestion, based on controlled rules acquired from expert knowledge and experimental evidence available in GlycoBase. The tool allows the targeted design of glycosidase enzyme mixtures by allowing researchers to model the action of exoglycosidases, thereby validating and improving the efficiency and accuracy of glycan analysis.","authors":[{"name":"Abrahams J.L."},{"name":"Campbell M.P."},{"name":"Gotz L."},{"name":"Karlsson N.G."},{"name":"Lisacek F."},{"name":"Mariethoz J."},{"name":"Packer N.H."},{"name":"Rudd P.M."}],"citationCount":25,"date":"2014-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"GlycoDigest: A tool for the targeted use of exoglycosidase digestions in glycan structure determination"},"pmcid":"PMC4609004","pmid":"25015990","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Enzymes","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0821"},{"term":"Proteomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0121"},{"term":"Small molecules","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0154"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"GlycoDigest","home":"https://bio.tools/glycodigest","summary":"Tool that simulates the action of these exoglycosidases on released oligosaccharides. It assists glycobiologists in designing enzyme mixtures that can be used to guide the precise determination of glycan structures.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:glycodigest/app/www.glycodigest.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":false,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":14,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2021"},{"count":1,"year":"2022"},{"count":3,"year":"2017"},{"count":3,"year":"2018"},{"count":3,"year":"2019"},{"count":3,"year":"2020"}],"doi":"10.1